# Copy this to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
#
# In-repo Pi extensions (`obsidian-vault`, `server`, `trade-journal`)
# auto-load this file at startup via `.pi/lib/dotenv.ts`, and
# `scripts/setup.sh` sources it before `npm run build`. So uncommenting a
# line below is usually enough — no need to source the file manually.
#
# Shell-exported values still take precedence, so you can override on the
# fly with:
#
#   AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_TITLE=experimental pi
#
# Note: `AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_TITLE` is read at BUILD time (it's baked into
# the static Nextra HTML). Re-run `bash scripts/setup.sh` (or
# `cd .pi/server && npm run build`) after changing it.

# ---- agents-team paths -----------------------------------------------------
# Override the default project-root vault location if you want notes to land
# in your real Obsidian vault elsewhere on disk.
# AGENTS_TEAM_VAULT_PATH=/Users/you/Obsidian/your-vault

# Relocate the Next.js + Nextra server (renders + PDFs). Defaults to
# <repo>/.pi/server.
# AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_PATH=/Users/you/agents-team-server

# Port the dev server binds. Default 8080.
# AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_PORT=8080

# Wordmark shown in the top-left of the Nextra navbar (and used as the page
# title suffix). Default "agents-team".
# AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_TITLE=my-notes

# Base URL the render / export tools return. Default http://localhost:8080.
# Set to your **named** cloudflared tunnel hostname so URLs are share-ready
# across sessions. Quick-tunnel URLs rotate on every restart and would go
# stale within hours.
# AGENTS_TEAM_SERVER_PUBLIC_URL=https://renders.example.com

# Override the Chrome binary used for PDF export. Auto-detected on macOS,
# Linux, and Windows. Set this if Chrome / Chromium lives somewhere else.
# AGENTS_TEAM_CHROME_PATH=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
